1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,700
Three brothers drew lots for the universe.

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:05,800
Their three sisters
were never given a lot.

3
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:08,820
All six had the same father.

4
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:13,999
Cronus had been warned that one of his
children would overthrow him, so he

5
00:00:13,999 --> 00:00:18,740
swallowed each of them at birth — the
daughters first: Hestia, Demeter and Hera.

6
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:21,940
Only the youngest, Zeus,
was hidden from him.

7
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:25,700
Grown, he forced his father to
bring them all back up, alive.

8
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,020
Together they beat the Titans.

9
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:31,400
Then the brothers divided
the prize: the sky to Zeus,

10
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,620
the sea to Poseidon, the dead to Hades.

11
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:37,840
The full story of that draw
is in the previous part.

12
00:00:37,860 --> 00:00:39,500
The sisters got no kingdom.

13
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:43,680
They got something smaller,
and closer to home: a marriage,

14
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:46,760
a harvest, and a fire in
the middle of the house.

15
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:48,680
Hera married the winner.

16
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:52,022
She became queen of the gods
and goddess of marriage —

17
00:00:52,022 --> 00:00:55,160
married to the least faithful
husband in Greek myth.

18
00:00:56,020 --> 00:01:01,060
She could not punish Zeus, so she went after
the women he loved, and their children.

19
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,280
Once she had Zeus put to sleep and
sent a storm after his son Heracles.

20
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:08,600
Zeus woke in a rage.

21
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:10,180
He hung her from the sky,

22
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:14,200
a golden chain on her wrists
and two anvils tied to her feet.

23
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:17,420
And yet the Greeks never
treated her as the loser.

24
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:20,060
At Olympia, Zeus's own sanctuary,

25
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:23,460
her temple stood for more
than a century before his.

26
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:29,912
And in one town in Arcadia she had three
shrines: to Hera the Girl, Hera the Wife,

27
00:01:29,912 --> 00:01:35,980
and Hera the Widow — from the time she
quarrelled with Zeus and went home.

28
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:39,440
A widow, with a husband
who could never die.

29
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,120
Demeter got the grain.

30
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:44,440
With Zeus she had a daughter, Persephone.

31
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:48,600
One day the girl was picking
flowers when the ground split open,

32
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,860
and Hades drove up in a golden chariot
and carried her down to the dead.

33
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:58,280
Zeus, her own father, had promised her
to him — without a word to her mother.

34
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:03,060
For nine days Demeter searched the
earth with a torch in each hand,

35
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,740
without eating or washing.

36
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:09,220
Then the Sun, who sees
everything, told her the truth.

37
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,600
Hades was her own brother,
he said, a fitting husband —

38
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:16,000
lord of the third share he drew
when the world was divided.

39
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:18,600
She did not accept it.

40
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,300
She left Olympus, sat down in her temple
at Eleusis, and stopped the grain.

41
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:29,960
For a whole year nothing grew; oxen dragged
ploughs through the fields for nothing.

42
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:34,940
Mankind was starving, and the gods
were about to lose their sacrifices.

43
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:41,040
Zeus sent a messenger, then every god on
Olympus, one after another, bearing gifts.

44
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:43,220
She refused them all.

45
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:45,760
Nothing would grow until
she saw her daughter.

46
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:48,180
And the king of the sky gave in.

47
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:51,263
He sent Hermes to bring Persephone back,

48
00:02:51,263 --> 00:02:55,840
and Hades let her go — but first he
slipped her a single pomegranate seed.

49
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,200
She had eaten in the land of the dead,

50
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:01,560
so for a third of every
year she would return below.

51
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:05,680
Only then did Demeter let
the fields grow again.

52
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:10,000
The sister with no kingdom had
made the king of the sky back down,

53
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,100
and the king of the dead
give back what he had taken.

54
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:15,600
Hestia got the fire.

55
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,460
She was the first child Cronus
swallowed, and the last to come back up.

56
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:24,160
Poseidon and Apollo
both asked to marry her.

57
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:28,740
She laid her hand on Zeus's head
and swore never to marry at all.

58
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:33,720
So instead of a husband, Zeus gave her
a place: the middle of every house.

59
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:38,720
The first offering at every
feast went to her, and the last.

60
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:43,620
Greek cities kept a public
hearth, and when colonists sailed

61
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:47,340
off to found a new city, they
carried its fire with them.

62
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,160
She has almost no myths of her own.

63
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:55,380
In Plato, when the gods ride out
across heaven, Hestia alone stays home.

64
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:59,940
The brothers drew three places
where no living person can stay.

65
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:03,500
The sisters got the
places where people live.

66
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:06,460
Every human life ends in Hades' kingdom.

67
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:08,220
It is lived in theirs.

68
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:12,399
The sisters were given no
kingdom — only the marriage,

69
00:04:12,399 --> 00:04:16,660
the harvest and the hearth that
every home is built around.

70
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:21,110
In the next part, three gods
who were never supposed to

71
00:04:21,110 --> 00:04:24,940
be born — one of them straight
out of her father's head.

72
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:30,640
Marriage, harvest or hearth —
which sister held the real power?

73
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,860
Tell us in the comments.

74
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:37,340
If you like stories like this one, leave
a like and subscribe to Animated Tales.

75
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:38,460
Until next time.
